{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"APPROVED design (from cranial-goodly-seahog escaped-bug deep-dive; user-approved 2026-08-18). Two grounded false-negatives drove this:\n\nCITRIC-PREREGAL-LADYBIRD (impact undercount): matched finding [regression, deletion-impact, tests] scored validity=1.0, impact=0.30, priority=0.30 — below deletion-impact@0.60 / api-compat@0.51. Removed PUBLIC API rebar.llm.review_ticket() was labeled capability_degraded+reachable_path_without_automated_coverage (MODERATE 0.6) not unversioned_published_contract_break (SERIOUS 0.9); trigger_likelihood=rare (prod x0.25); churn90=0 (maint freq_mult x0.5). Reproduced exactly: correcting ANY one -> impact 0.60 (clears both).\n\nBRATTISH-LADYISH-JAGUAR (validity drop + zero impact): [regression, edge-cases] finding at _build-and-test.yml:123 dropped at validity 0.4286 (<0.5), evidence_entails_finding=no + several insufficient; every consequence binary false -> impact 0.0. Pure pass-2 recall failure on a workflow-YAML artifact.\n\nAPPROVED CHANGES:\n(a1) freq_mult reshape — churn AMPLIFY-ONLY, never suppress. Reshape freq_mult from [0.5..1.0] to [1.0..1.x] so a hot file boosts a maintainability finding but a cold/NEW file (churn90=0 includes every brand-new file) never discounts it below its intrinsic tier. AND never let the frequency multiplier reduce a SERIOUS-tier binary. This subsumes the contract-break case and kills the general new/quiet-file FN class without per-criterion exceptions (see decide.impact_code freq_mult, workflow_ops._churn_90d = git log --since=90d count).\n(a2) version-signal gating — classify unversioned_published_contract_break SERIOUS only when the removal LACKS a version/deprecation signal (major bump / deprecation cycle / CHANGELOG breaking-change). Managed removals do not trip; unmanaged ones flag (correct: client usage is unobservable). Resolution paths: add version/deprecation; scope-intent context (note code-review has NO auto on-target veto); fp_ledger fp:code-review NO-FIRE case.\n(proposal-3, approved earlier) pass-2 removed-public-symbol sub-question — key detection on the EXPORT (name reachable from the public API: __all__/re-export, CLI command, MCP tool), NOT on a cited caller. Absence of an internal caller does not prove an external API unused.\nPass-3 validity<0.5 hard-drop stays impact-blind (making it impact-aware resurrects noise and would not have saved brattish — impact was 0.0); the lever is pass-2 recall/labeling, not the floor."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787077837213670001,"uuid":"6be9180d-ef90-4502-a4b6-677d9e72ad2a"}